  "content": "[Verse 1]\n[D]They disembarked in fourty five\n[G]And noone spoke and noone smiled\n[A]There were to many spaces in the line.\n[D]And\ngathered at the cenotaph\n[G]All agreed with hand on heart\n[A]To sheath the sacrificial Knifes.\n[D]But now She\n\n[Verse 2]\n[D]stands upon Southampton dock With her\n[G]handkerchief And her summer frock\n[A]clings To her wet body in the rain.\n[D]In\nquiet desperation knuckles\n[G]White upon the slippery reins She\n[A]bravely waves the boys Goodbye again.\n[D]Mmm.\n[G]  [Gm]\n[D]\n[D]  [Em7]  [D/A]\n\n[Verse 3]\n[G]And still the dark stain\nspreads between Their\n[D]shoulder blades.\n[G]A mute re-\nminder of the\n[D]poppy fields and graves.\n[G]When the fight was\n[A]over We\n[D]spent what [F#m7]they had\n[Bm]made. But\n\n[Outro]\n[Em7]in the bottom of our hearts We felt the final\n[D]cut.",
